+# aider chat started at 2026-10-15 00:07:51
+
+> ~/.local/bin/aider --model openai/bench-model --yes-always --no-auto-commits --no-check-update --analytics-disable --no-show-model-warnings --no-pretty --no-stream --no-gitignore --message str() on the pytest.raises context variable doesn't behave same as normal exception catch
+Pytest 4.6.2, macOS 10.14.5
+
+```Python
+try:
+    raise LookupError(
+        f"A\n"
+        f"B\n"
+        f"C"
+    )
+except LookupError as e:
+    print(str(e))
+```
+prints
+
+> A
+> B
+> C
+
+But
+
+```Python
+with pytest.raises(LookupError) as e:
+    raise LookupError(
+        f"A\n"
+        f"B\n"
+        f"C"
+    )
+
+print(str(e))
+```
+
+prints
+
+> <console>:3: LookupError: A
+
+In order to get the full error message, one must do `str(e.value)`, which is documented, but this is a different interaction. Any chance the behavior could be changed to eliminate this gotcha?
