+changelog/5467.bugfix.rst
+```
+``ExceptionInfo`` now returns the exception string when calling ``str()`` on it, matching
+the behavior of ``str()`` on regular exceptions (e.g. ``str(exception)``). In order to obtain
+the previous string representation (which included the traceback location) use
+``str(excinfo.getrepr())`` or ``excinfo.traceback`` instead.
+```
+
+The fix changes `ExceptionInfo.__str__` to return `str(self._excinfo[1])` (i.e. `str(self.value)`) instead of formatting the exception info as `<path>:<lineno>: <ExceptionType>: <first line of message>`. This matches Python's normal exception behavior where `str(e)` returns the full exception message.
+
+I've also updated `test_excinfo_str` to assert the new behavior (verifying that `str(excinfo) == str(excinfo.value)`, including a multiline message case that would have failed with the old behavior), and added a changelog entry.
